{"name":"Frangipane","hex":"#f4d5b2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"frangipane","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cream made from ground almonds used in confectionery","A pastry filled with this cream"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frangipane"}],"entries":[{"title":"Frangipane","blocks":[{"text":"Frangipane is a sweet almond-flavoured cream typical in French patisserie. Frangipane is used in a variety of ways, including cakes and such pastries as the Bakewell tart, conversation tart, Jésuite, and galette des rois. The first written record was in a French cookbook from 1674, where it was spelt franchipane, and was described as a custard tart flavoured with pounded almonds and pistachios. However, food historian Claudine Brecourt-Villars, writing in 1996, says, in her view, frangipane meant cream. Alan Davidson, in his book The Oxford Companion to Food, called Frangipane an almond based mixture."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Frangipane.jpg/330px-Frangipane.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frangipane"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Gros_plan_de_galette_des_rois_2013.jpg/500px-Gros_plan_de_galette_des_rois_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Gros_plan_de_galette_des_rois_2013.jpg/1280px-Gros_plan_de_galette_des_rois_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Gros_plan_de_galette_des_rois_2013.jpg/500px-Gros_plan_de_galette_des_rois_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"French galette des rois (kings' cake)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGros_plan_de_galette_des_rois_2013.jpg"}],"soun